{:edb/db-before-t 2317 :edb/db-after-t 2318 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535630 50 #inst "2026-10-09T03:57:37.027Z" 13194139535630 true] [17592186124506 1020 #edb/ref 17592186358343 13194139535630 true] [17592186124506 1020 #edb/ref 17592186358357 13194139535630 true] [17592186124506 1020 #edb/ref 17592186358364 13194139535630 true] [17592186124507 1020 #edb/ref 17592186358336 13194139535630 true] [17592186124507 1020 #edb/ref 17592186358350 13194139535630 true] [17592186358336 1017 #edb/ref 17592186358337 13194139535630 true] [17592186358336 1089 "q-176835" 13194139535630 true] [17592186358336 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535630 true] [17592186358336 1100 "Given that the intersection of the elliptic cone $4(x+3)^{2}+8(y-1)^{2}=(z+7)^{2}$ and the plane $z=-3$ is an ellipse, what is the length of its major axis?" 13194139535630 true] [17592186358336 1113 #uuid "b96d3db6-3bd4-5dd7-9484-9554529374d1" 13194139535630 true] [17592186358336 1145 "To find the intersection of the elliptic cone and the plane $z=-3,$ we substitute $z=-3$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(x+3)^{2}+8(y-1)^{2} & =(-3+7)^{2} \\\\ 4(x+3)^{2}+8(y-1)^{2} & ={4}^{2} \\\\ 4(x+3)^{2}+8(y-1)^{2} & =16 \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{(2)^{2}}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of an ellipse with a semi-major axis of length $a=2.$ Therefore, the major axis has length $2a=4.$" 13194139535630 true] [17592186358337 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358338 13194139535630 true] [17592186358337 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358339 13194139535630 true] [17592186358337 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358340 13194139535630 true] [17592186358337 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358341 13194139535630 true] [17592186358337 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358342 13194139535630 true] [17592186358337 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535630 true] [17592186358337 1041 "selection" 13194139535630 true] [17592186358337 1104 #edb/ref 17592186358342 13194139535630 true] [17592186358337 1110 #uuid "d225e5c8-4d5a-5189-b8b6-41c036c699a4" 13194139535630 true] [17592186358338 1034 "\\sqrt{2}" 13194139535630 true] [17592186358338 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535630 true] [17592186358338 1111 #uuid "a604bc03-6712-5fa8-888d-872bf83b126e" 13194139535630 true] [17592186358339 1034 "16" 13194139535630 true] [17592186358339 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535630 true] [17592186358339 1111 #uuid "0b320a2e-92d8-52d4-b617-2a8f70b0421e" 13194139535630 true] [17592186358340 1034 "8" 13194139535630 true] [17592186358340 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535630 true] [17592186358340 1111 #uuid "cefba145-4076-5b1a-aaf4-c6cc40a50274" 13194139535630 true] [17592186358341 1034 "6" 13194139535630 true] [17592186358341 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535630 true] [17592186358341 1111 #uuid "ad076e91-5f00-51fe-8611-2b87707fb879" 13194139535630 true] [17592186358342 1034 "4" 13194139535630 true] [17592186358342 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535630 true] [17592186358342 1111 #uuid "d0416f8b-a1ef-546a-9011-ccdc83b6c7ba" 13194139535630 true] [17592186358343 1017 #edb/ref 17592186358344 13194139535630 true] [17592186358343 1089 "q-94485" 13194139535630 true] [17592186358343 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535630 true] [17592186358343 1100 "Given the elliptic cone $\\frac{(x-6)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{8}=\\frac{(z+6)^{2}}{6},$ find its intercepts with the $y$-axis." 13194139535630 true] [17592186358343 1113 #uuid "2e9f175e-8026-51c8-a30f-c784766388ba" 13194139535630 true] [17592186358343 1145 "To find the $y$-intercepts of the elliptic cone, we plug $x=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(0-6)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{8} & =\\frac{(0+6)^{2}}{6} \\\\ \\frac{36}{9}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{8} & =\\frac{36}{6} \\\\ 4+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{8} & =6 \\\\ \\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{8} & =2 \\\\ (y-4)^{2} & =16 \\\\ y-4 & =\\pm 4 \\\\ y & =4\\pm 4 \\\\ y & =0,8\\end{aligned}